.TH VID2GIF 1 "July 2026" "vid2gif 2.0.0"
.SH NAME
vid2gif \- convert a video file into an animated GIF file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vid2gif
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIinput\fR [\fIoutput\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vid2gif
uses FFmpeg to make an animated GIF from a video file. It generates a palette
for the GIF, applies the requested filters, and optimizes the result with
.B image_optim
when that program is installed.

When \fIoutput\fR is omitted, vid2gif uses the input filename with a
.I .gif
extension. The Homebrew formula also installs
.B movie2gif
as a compatibility alias.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a , " --time-scale " \fIfactor\fR
Set the FFmpeg presentation-time factor. Values below 1 speed up the GIF;
values above 1 slow it down.
.TP
.BR \-c , " --colors " \fIcount\fR
Set palette colours. The default is 32.
.TP
.BR \-C , " --crop " \fIfilter\fR
Apply a crop filter in FFmpeg's \fIout_w:out_h:x:y\fR form. The legacy
.B -o
spelling is also accepted.
.TP
.BR \-d , " --duration " \fIseconds\fR
Limit the converted duration.
.TP
.BR \-f , " --filters " \fIfilters\fR
Replace all generated FFmpeg filters.
.TP
.BR \-i , " --interactive"
Always ask before overwriting an existing output.
.TP
.BR \-m , " --append-filter " \fIfilters\fR
Append FFmpeg filters to the generated filter chain.
.TP
.BR \-n , " --dry-run"
Print commands without writing files.
.TP
.BR \-N , " --no-overwrite"
Refuse to overwrite an existing output.
.TP
.BR \-O , " --optim, --optimize"
Require \fBimage_optim\fR to optimize the finished GIF. The command fails if
the optimizer is unavailable.
.TP
.BR "--no-optim, --no-optimize"
Do not run \fBimage_optim\fR.
.B +O
is a shorthand for this option.
.TP
.BR "--auto-optim, --auto-optimize"
Run \fBimage_optim\fR when it is available. This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-p , " --palette " \fIfile\fR
Use or write the specified palette PNG.
.TP
.BR \-r , " --fps " \fIfps\fR
Set output frame rate. The default is 10.
.TP
.BR \-s , " --start " \fIseconds\fR
Set input start time.
.TP
.BR \-H , " --height " \fIpixels\fR
Set output height. The default is \fI-1\fR, which preserves aspect ratio. The
legacy \fB-t\fR alias is also accepted.
.TP
.BR \-v , " --version"
Show script name and version number.
.TP
.BR \-V , " --verbose"
Show FFmpeg commands and settings.
.TP
.BR \-w , " --width " \fIpixels\fR
Set output width. The default is 720.
.TP
.BR \-y , " --overwrite"
Overwrite an existing output without asking.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B ffmpeg
Generates the palette and GIF.
.TP
.B ImageMagick
Adjusts the palette. The \fBmagick\fR or \fBmogrify\fR command is required.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Convert a video:
.nf
.B vid2gif input.mp4
.fi
.TP
Convert a five-second clip starting at three seconds:
.nf
.B vid2gif -s 3 -d 5 input.mp4 clip.gif
.fi
.TP
Preview generated commands without writing files:
.nf
.B vid2gif --dry-run input.mp4
.fi
